# Compiled bytecode is regenerated on every import and is never an input to any
# model. Tracking it meant the working tree went dirty after every healthcheck
# run, which is what made "commit your changes" fire on a repo nobody had edited.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# packaging / editable-install metadata
*.egg-info/

# Mutation-harness temp copies. `--mutants` writes a patched copy of a module into harness/ (it has
# to live there for imports to resolve), runs its selftest, and unlinks it. They exist for a second
# or two each, but a suite running dozens of them leaves the tree looking dirty to any check that
# samples at the wrong moment — and an independent review running several suites at once makes that
# routine. Never an input to anything; never committed.
harness/tmp*_mutant.py
harness/_dbg_*.py
